/* Distributed Compute Playground — component catalogue (Apache Spark family).
 * Facts follow the "What actually happens when you call spark.read?" article and the
 * Spark 3.5 / 4.0 documentation. Defaults are Spark's unless a component changes them.
 *
 * Component fields
 *   id, b ('spark'), slot, n (name), icon, d (description)
 *   base      – execution engines only: starting capability scores
 *   fx        – capability deltas applied when the component is active
 *   needs     – { any: [ids], msg } prerequisite; fx not applied if unmet
 *   engines   – execution engines this component works with (unset = all)
 *   conflicts – [{ id, msg }]
 *   flavors   – platforms that offer it: 'OSS' | 'Dataproc' | 'EMR' | 'Databricks' (unset = all)
 *   note      – { lvl: 'info' | 'warn' | 'danger', t }
 *   caps      – capability sentences unlocked when active
 *   conf      – spark-defaults / --conf lines; code – PySpark lines
 *   sim       – knobs read by the job simulator (see core/engine.js)
 */
